            "output": "<path>/Users/nickdejesus/Code/nimbus/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Nimbus\n2: \n3: Nimbus runs checkpoint-aware cloud review workflows so you can review code at a known Entire commit state with one command.\n4: \n5: ## Quick Start (Hosted Nimbus)\n6: \n7: Prereqs:\n8: \n9: - Node 20+\n10: - A repo tracked with Entire checkpoints\n11: - Nimbus API key (provided by Nimbus admin)\n12: - GitHub PAT for your repo (used as `REVIEW_CONTEXT_GITHUB_TOKEN`)\n13: \n14: Install:\n15: \n16: ```bash\n17: npm install -g @dayhaysoos/nimbus\n18: ```\n19: \n20: Set local environment variables:\n21: \n22: ```bash\n23: export NIMBUS_WORKER_URL=\"https://nimbus-worker.ndejesus1227.workers.dev\"\n24: export NIMBUS_API_KEY=\"nmb_live_...\"\n25: ```\n26: \n27: ### Onboard a New Repository (one-time)\n28: \n29: 1. Register your repo to your Nimbus account:\n30: \n31: ```bash\n32: nimbus repo register --repo owner/repo\n33: ```\n34: \n35: 2. Add your GitHub PAT to repository secrets:\n36:    - Secret name: `REVIEW_CONTEXT_GITHUB_TOKEN`\n37:    - Location: Repo Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions\n38: \n39: 3. Add the Nimbus PR workflow file to your repo:\n40:    - `.github/workflows/nimbus-pr-review.yml`\n41: \n42: 4. Open or update a PR.\n43:    - Nimbus runs automatically.\n44:    - A successful run posts a Nimbus findings comment on the PR.\n45: \n46: Notes:\n47: \n48: - `NIMBUS_API_KEY` is for local CLI use (for example, `repo register`).\n49: - CI uses short-lived runtime tokens and should not require storing a long-lived Nimbus API key secret.\n50: - Reviews can still run without `REVIEW_CONTEXT_GITHUB_TOKEN`, but co-change context may be unavailable and review quality can drop.\n51: \n52: Run your first local review:\n53: \n54: ```bash\n55: nimbus review create --commit HEAD\n56: ```\n57: \n58: Want the full walkthrough and troubleshooting? See `docs/getting-started.md`.\n59: \n60: ## How It Works\n61: \n62: Nimbus resolves your commit and Entire checkpoint context, creates an isolated workspace, runs deployment checks in Cloudflare Sandbox, and then creates a non-mutating review report. The CLI streams progress in real time and returns a report URL when complete. Review output includes findings, severity, and provenance so you can understand both what changed and why the review reached its recommendation.\n63: \n64: ## Self-hosting\n65: \n66: Nimbus supports hosted usage and self-hosted worker deployments. For setup steps, runtime requirements, and local dev workflow, see `docs/development.md`.\n67: \n68: ## License\n69: \n70: MIT\n\n(End of file - total 70 lines)\n</content>",
