        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Title: Entire enabled but commits never get `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer (hooks run, no linkage)\n\nHi Entire team — we’re seeing a reproducible issue where Entire is enabled and hooks are installed, but new commits do not receive `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers.\n\nContext:\n- Repo: `dayhaysoos/nimbus`\n- Branch: `policy-e2e-verify-nochange`\n- Entire version: `0.5.1`\n- Shell/OS: macOS + zsh\n- Agent mode: OpenCode / manual-commit\n\nWhy this is blocking:\n- Our review pipeline requires commit prompt-history provenance from `Entire-Checkpoint`.\n- Without trailer attachment, all review flows hard-fail (by design).\n\nReproduction steps:\n1. Ensure Entire is enabled and hooks installed:\n   ```bash\n   entire enable --force --absolute-git-hook-path --agent opencode\n   entire status\n   ls -l .git/hooks/prepare-commit-msg .git/hooks/commit-msg .git/hooks/post-commit\n   ```\n2. Make/stage any file change.\n3. Commit with debug:\n   ```bash\n   ENTIRE_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG git commit -m \"checkpoint debug test\"\n   ```\n4. Check commit linkage:\n   ```bash\n   git show -s --format=%B HEAD\n   entire explain --commit HEAD --no-pager\n   entire trace\n   ```\n\nObserved behavior:\n- Commit succeeds, but commit message has no trailer:\n  - no `Entire-Checkpoint: ...`\n- `entire explain --commit HEAD --no-pager` returns:\n  - `No associated Entire checkpoint`\n  - `Commit <sha> does not have an Entire-Checkpoint trailer.`\n- `entire trace` only shows post-commit:\n  - `post-commit ...`\n  - step: `open_repository_and_head`\n- `entire doctor` reports metadata branches OK (no obvious repair action suggested).\n\nAdditional notes:\n- `entire resume policy-e2e-verify-nochange` says:\n  - `No Entire checkpoint found on branch 'policy-e2e-verify-nochange'`\n- This creates a deadlock: no checkpoint on branch -> cannot resume; commit path still does not create one.\n\nExpected behavior:\n- With Entire enabled and hooks installed, `git commit` should attach an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer (or provide explicit failure output explaining why linking was skipped and how to recover).\n\nActual behavior:\n- Commits are created silently without checkpoint trailer, despite enabled status and installed hooks.\n\nWhat we’d love from Entire:\n1. Guidance on required preconditions for checkpoint attachment in manual-commit mode.\n2. Why only `post-commit` appears in trace while trailer injection does not occur.\n3. A deterministic recovery path when branch has zero checkpointed commits.\n4. Optional hard-fail mode: abort commit if checkpoint cannot be attached.\n\nIf helpful, I can provide exact commit SHAs and full command output transcript.",
