          "type": "text",
          "text": "You were right to flag it — I found the concrete break.\n\n- Entire hooks were actually missing from `.git/hooks` (only `*.sample` existed), so no trailer could ever be added.\n- That’s why `entire status` said enabled but commits had no checkpoint and `entire trace` was empty/useless.\n- I reinstalled hooks with:\n  - `entire enable --force --absolute-git-hook-path --agent opencode`\n- Verified these now exist and are executable:\n  - `.git/hooks/prepare-commit-msg`\n  - `.git/hooks/commit-msg`\n  - `.git/hooks/post-commit`\n\nI also cleaned up your index so you don’t accidentally commit Entire config churn:\n- Restored `.entire/.gitignore` and `.entire/settings.json`\n- Unstaged `.entire/settings.local.json`\n- Current staged change is only `README.md`\n\nNow run this exact test commit:\n\n```bash\nENTIRE_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG git commit -m \"testing entire hooks after reinstall\"\ngit show -s --format=%B HEAD\nentire explain --commit HEAD --no-pager\nentire trace\n```\n\nIf this still doesn’t add a trailer, paste those 4 outputs and I’ll pinpoint the next blocker immediately.",
