        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Great question. Based on all the evidence, I think there are **two different failure modes** happening:\n\n- **Mode 1: no trailer added**  \n  - Log shows: `prepare-commit-msg: no content to link`  \n  - This means Entire sees hooks, but can’t match the staged commit content to an active session payload.\n- **Mode 2: trailer added but checkpoint missing**  \n  - My canary got `Entire-Checkpoint: 1c9dfafc4479`, but `entire explain` says `checkpoint not found`.\n  - That means injection happened, but checkpoint persistence/lookup is inconsistent.\n\nWhy “I can sometimes create one but you can’t”:\n- Entire appears to be **session-link sensitive**.  \n- Commits linked to the currently active captured session may get a trailer; commits outside that exact session context may not.\n- Your logs also showed transcript prep errors (`opencode export returned invalid JSON`), which can break session/checkpoint materialization even when hooks run.\n\nSo yes — you’re right: both of us should be able to do it reliably, and right now Entire is not deterministic.\n\nIf you want, next I can give you a strict 60-second “single known-good checkpoint test” script and we’ll run it once to produce a definitive pass/fail artifact for Entire.",
