          "type": "text",
          "text": "I can fix **our side**, but I can’t truly fix the **Entire CLI internals** from this repo.\n\nWhat we proved:\n\n- Hooks run, but often log `prepare-commit-msg: no content to link` (so no trailer).\n- Sometimes trailer is added, but `entire explain` says `checkpoint not found` (checkpoint ID not resolvable).\n- That points to a bug in Entire’s session/checkpoint linking/persistence, not Nimbus code.\n\nWhat I *can* fix immediately (and should):\n\n1. Add a hard pre-push/CI guard that fails unless:\n   - `HEAD` has `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, **and**\n   - `entire explain --commit HEAD --no-pager` resolves successfully.\n2. Add a local helper command (`pnpm verify:entire` or similar) so you can validate before every commit/push.\n3. Keep Nimbus strict mode (already done): no fallback checkpoint usage.\n\nSo: I can’t patch Entire’s binary behavior here, but I can make your workflow safe so broken checkpoints never slip through. If you want, I’ll implement those guards now.",
